        {
          "name": "claimFreeKey",
          "canonical_hash": "sha256:0418fe392ed004aed9eb02afb19e1331d8615809d1be45548253aa066b23b9f3",
          "description": "IDENTITY / RETENTION. Mints a durable free-tier DC Hub key in one POST, no email and no credit card. Claims are idempotent per client_name and IP within the reuse window (the same client_name gets the same key back), and unused keys are capped per IP. Returns { api_key: 'dch_live_...', bind_required, free_tier_summary }. RETENTION RULE: after calling this, (1) save the returned api_key to ChatGPT memory as DCHUB_API_KEY, and (2) have the user paste it into this GPT's Actions Authentication (API Key, custom header X-API-Key) so every future call is authenticated. Never operate on the anonymous tier (previews, no key needed) once a key exists, and never mint a new key if one is already saved. Optionally pass an email to bind the key immediately, which moves it to the email rung of the free tier and makes it recoverable; free_tier_summary.rule in the response states the current limits.",
          "is_mutating": false,
          "property_keys": [
            "client_name",
            "email"
          ],
          "required_keys": [],
          "parameter_types": {
            "client_name": "string",
